WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.150
In 2018, a UK advisory body
looked at a heated question.

2
00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:08.030
Do migrants take local people's jobs?

3
00:00:08.030 --> 00:00:11.070
It found no or little
impact on the overall

4
00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:15.940
employment of UK-born workers,
though effects may differ by skill.

5
00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:19.300
Yet in many places, jobs
sit empty while people

6
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.190
elsewhere look for work.

7
00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:23.610
Why can jobs sit empty in one place while

8
00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:26.330
people elsewhere cannot find work?

9
00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:29.260
In this mission, you'll
uncover the barriers that keep

10
00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:31.060
workers from the jobs.

11
00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:33.400
Then you'll use a graph lab to test what

12
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.870
really happens to wages
when new workers arrive.

13
00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:41.580
Your mission: find out why jobs
and job seekers can stay apart,

14
00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:43.470
and what could bring them together.
